-- Inert as rules of cover: Article 35 disclaims a duty to verify payments and reserves measures
-- against money laundering; Article 36 imposes a duty to notify immediately and in
-- writing, with no stated consequence. The duty is stated, without a clock.
@ref Article 36 (src 1186-1201)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Act under the contract`
`Article 36 — the duty to notify a United States tax matter` MEANS
    PARTY `the policyowner`
    MUST  `notify the Company in writing of a United States tax matter`

§§ `Article 37 — deduction of unpaid amounts`

-- src:1205 | 37. Khấu trừ Công ty có quyền khấu trừ các Khoản khấu trừ hàng tháng, khoản phí đến
-- src:1210 | các khoản chưa hạn nhưng chưa được thanh toán trước khi chi trả bất kỳ quyền lợi bảo hiểm
-- src:1211 | thanh toán nào hoặc khi Khách hàng yêu cầu chấm dứt Hợp đồng bảo hiểm trước hạn.
-- The Company may deduct due and unpaid monthly deductions and premiums before paying any benefit
-- or the value on early termination. LAW: Article 37(4) of the Law on Insurance Business forbids
-- deducting premiums from the surrender value without consent (fork L5).
@ref Article 37 (src 1205-1211)
GIVEN `the unpaid amounts`   IS A NUMBER
      `the amount payable`   IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Article 37 — what is paid after deducting unpaid amounts of` `the unpaid amounts` `from` `the amount payable` MEANS
    IF   `the amount payable` MINUS `the unpaid amounts` LESS THAN 0
    THEN `the refund is less than nothing, and the document does not say what follows`
    ELSE `the amount payable` MINUS `the unpaid amounts`

